  "chain": "replacement D87 timer introduces ~15ms delay, eliminating design margin [cause B] -> BO logic inadvertently actuates during load sequencer reset -> 2ETB switchgear de-energized/load shed -> unplanned actuation of 2B Emergency AC Electrical Power System; in parallel BO actuation -> unplanned actuation of 2B AFW System (steam supply valves open, MD AFW pump loaded)",
  "golden_questions": [
    "Q1",
    "Q3",
    "Q4",
    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "Two parallel consequences (AC power system actuation and AFW system actuation) both trace to the same BO logic inadvertent actuation failure mode, occurring on two separate test portions (SI-only on 9/13 causing switchgear de-energization; SI-concurrent-with-BO on 9/12 causing AFW steam valve actuation only, since 2ETB was already being fed by the 2B DG). No previous similar occurrence LER was identified per the narrative ('No previous similar events were identified within the past five years'), so no stub LER/SIMILAR_TO edge was created. Turbine-driven AFW pump was not itself actuated (design blocks it during coincident SI), so only steam supply valves and the motor-driven AFW pump are modeled as affected AFW components. EK and BA systems are modeled because the event directly involved/actuated them, not merely as design-context mentions."
}